# Everything `regenerate.sh` produces.
#
# The four recordings, the four ORIGINAL modules the offline replay is
# driven against (spec §6.1), and the `expected.json` answers the page
# observed are NOT committed. The modules were, on the grounds that a
# recording pins export names, import indices and — for `vault_apply` —
# the absolute address of its `VAULT` block, so a module built by a
# different toolchain no longer describes the recording. Producing each
# module in the same run as its recording satisfies that properly, and
# additionally keeps the pair a description of the current instrumenter
# rather than of whichever one last ran.
#
# `scripts/materialize-recording.sh` records all four into the gitignored
# `target/test-recordings/`, keyed on this fixture's sources and on the
# content of `ct-instrument` and the browser recorder. The zstd step that
# squeezed each ~0.6 MB debug module under the repo's 500 KB commit cap is
# gone with the commit.
modules/*/*.ct/
modules/*/module/
modules/*/expected.json

# Build output.
modules/*/build/

# What the browser loads, written beside the page that serves it, built in
# the same run as the recording. The repo root's blanket `*.wasm` already
# ignores it; this is the statement of intent.
modules/*/page/*.instrumented.wasm
modules/*/page/*.instrumented.wasm.manifest.json
